 "stimulus_html": "Use the figure to answer the following exercises. In each exercise, a graph and a sequence of vertices are given. Determine whether each sequence of vertices is an Euler trail, an Euler circuit, or neither for the graph. If it is neither, explain why.\n<br>\n<figure><img src=\"exercises/media/71fc910ee654a36b.png\" alt=\"Four graphs. Graph A has two overlapping quadrilaterals, s t u v and w x y z. An edge connects w to u. Graph B has two overlapping quadrilaterals, s t z y, and r v w x. A vertex, u is at the center of r v and t z. Graph C has six vertices. The edges connect s t, t v, v w, w x, x u, w u, u s, and u t. Graph D has 10 vertices. The edges from t lead to x, r, s, u, and q. The edges from x lead to v, w, y, and z. The edges connect r s, u q, v w, and y z.\"></figure>\n",
